  "body": "## What changed\n\nRoot cause: Setup2 followed the document's machine (the default), so a pick on its Machine page routed to `LoadMachine` - the document's machine - which Setup1 also follows. Setup1 then read Setup2's pick: wrong travel and spindle refusals for Setup1 (Prime Directive).\n\n- `crates/ui/src/state_setup_mount.rs`: the machine verbs (library combo, Load other, Edit apply, Clear, Machines-pane \"Use for this setup\", ribbon mode switch) and the post pick route through `State::machine_target` / `post_target`: the active setup when it owns its mount (as before), or - new - when the document has **two or more setups**; then the pick is that setup's own (`SetSetupMachine` / `SetSetupPost`, the existing undoable commands). With no setups or one, the pick still sets the document's machine/post, unchanged.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_pages.rs`: the own/document group on the setup's Machine and Post pages says by name where a pick lands - \"A machine picked on this page is Setup2's own - no other setup changes.\" or \"... sets the document's machine - every setup without its own uses it.\"\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1515-setup-own-machine-pick.md` (rule chosen: two-or-more setups; dropped: \"only when another setup follows\", refuse-and-ask; MCP unchanged).\n\nMCP: `load_machine` already takes `setup` (that setup's own machine) and names the document explicitly without it, so an agent always states its target - no change. Parity is pinned by the existing `mcp_setup_mount_trace::a_setups_own_machine_picked_over_mcp_reaches_its_own_posted_file_and_undoes` (Setup1 keeps its VMC while Setup2 takes its own 770M; undo).\n\n## How tested\n\nNew `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_machine_bleed.rs` (pins, each mutation-checked):\n- `a_machine_picked_on_setup2_leaves_setup1_without_one` - the report: Setup1 no machine, pick on Setup2; Setup1 still none, Setup2 reads Lathe, document untouched, undo/redo walk both.\n- `verbs_on_setup2_never_move_setup1s_or_the_documents_machine` - document mill, Clear then pick on Setup2; Setup1 and the document keep the mill; two undos restore.\n- `with_one_setup_a_pick_still_sets_the_documents_machine` - single-setup behaviour unchanged.\n- `a_post_picked_on_setup2_leaves_setup1s_post` - the same law for the post pick.\n- `the_setup2_machine_page_says_and_does_its_own_pick` - real page: AccessKit label names Setup2's own, Library combo pick leaves Setup1 alone.\n- `the_only_setups_machine_page_names_the_documents_machine` - AccessKit label names the document's machine.\n\nMutations (each reverted): machine routing back to owner-only -> 3 fail; post routing owner-only -> post pin fails; single setup also binding own (`> 0`) -> 3 fail; page line always \"own\" -> 1 fails; page line removed -> 2 fail; `SetSetupMachine::invert` a no-op -> both undo pins fail.\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (ui lib 716 passed + 10 ui suites, 0.4 min; this run planned no clippy step). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNot exercised: a hand check in the GUI; the release-lane pixel snapshots (no PNG changed - the setup Machine/Post pages gain one text line, which may move a release-lane golden of those pages at the cut).\n\nFollow-up: #1526 (post OPTIONS keep the old own-or-document routing, same shape).\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (branch from upstream/main fd2f4f30).\n\nChangelog: With two or more setups, a machine or post picked on one setup's page becomes that setup's own and no longer changes another setup's machine or post; the page says where a pick lands (#1515)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1515\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
